bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    native_build_cold_init_admission_wall_386s_2026-11-07, 0, "2026-11-09 lane-p2-1 BLOCKED-EVIDENCE. Reproduced natively: stage2_new4.exe native-build --entry-closure of a 30-line single-file entry with SIMPLE_SCV_INVENTORY_COLD_INIT=1 took 631 s wall, of which the build phases (parse..mir) took ~20 s (build-trace elapsed_ms=19542 at mir) -> ~610 s is admission, worse than the 386 s seed figure. Two costs: (1) source_authority.spl:242-246 widens cold inventory_roots to src+test+examples/10_tooling, and _compiler_inventory_refresh_observed_cost_v1 documents that a cold refresh REPLACES the inventory so its roots must cover the whole scope (the warm cursor then requires untracked_src/test digests); (2) scv_compile_snapshot_acquire_cost_v2 materialises every file of the selectors (src/lib,src/app,src/compiler,src/os) into build/scv/snapshots. Scoping either to the entry closure changes the inventory/snapshot authority contract (partial-scope cursor, per-family generations) - a design decision, not a local patch. Missing: owner design for per-root cold inventory caching + a phase cost profile (the traced run was killed by the disk guard at 290 s, C: 4-8 GB free)."

